From b5982a37c72ab3bae07375de42b90ae8c93b89b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:52:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] irqchip: add Baochip bao1x interrupt controller drivers

The bao1x SoC's VexRiscv core has no PLIC or CLINT; external interrupts
arrive through a 32-line interrupt array (VexRiscv
ExternalInterruptArrayPlugin) controlled by custom supervisor CSRs:
0x9C0 masks lines, 0xDC0 reads pending state. The array line feeds the
hart's supervisor external interrupt, so irq-bao1x-intc chains off
riscv-intc hwirq 9 and dispatches by scanning 0xDC0. Lines are
level-type: sources latch and hold until acked at the source.

Most sources are behind IRQARRAY banks - LiteX EventManager-style
aggregators (up to 16 events each, EV_PENDING write-1-to-clear,
EV_ENABLE gate) that collapse a bank onto one array line.
irq-bao1x-irqarray models each bank as a chained edge-type domain.

Co-developed-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
